    "text": "The WorldLines paper introduces memory-to-plan translation solely within the system description for rebuilding world states under partial observability, without framing it as a standalone or universal challenge.",
    "topic": "scope of introduction"
  },
  {
    "text": "In the WorldLines paper, memory-to-plan translation is algorithmically coupled to the detection and resolution of overwritten memory states, not discussed as an agent-agnostic capability.",
    "topic": "technical coupling"
  },
  {
    "text": "The paper contains no explicit statement that memory-to-plan translation is a fundamental problem for all embodied agents, nor does it describe it outside the context of its specific architecture.",
    "topic": "generality claim"
  }
]
